 "name": "Daily",
 "_about": "Calm everyday layout: speed is the hero, with the gear on the left and the clock and oil on the right. Fitted (Nov 5 2026 grid photo) to the part of the HUD the driver sees, x 120..605, y 100..378, with a 6 px margin; the bottom-left x 150..355, y 314..378 is left to BMW's own speed and speed-limit sign, which it keeps drawing over ours in Comfort. To change it, copy this file into the app data folder layouts/ (scripts/deploy.sh); the app reloads it by itself. Widget types and tokens: see the header of hud.js. Modes (hud.js header): cruise moves everything to the right half, clear of BMW's ACC block (x ~240..345, y ~200..312) and speed; nav keeps a small column on the left (gear, clock, oil, x 126..305, y 172..290) under BMW's guidance line (y ~160) and clear of its turn map (x ~310..605); cruiseNav keeps gear, clock and oil in the sliver left of the ACC block. Measured off the Nov 7 2026 HUD photos, not the grid: check on the car. In cruise a row under the oil shows the car ahead: GAP ({{accGap}}) and REL ({{accRel}}), raw until config.acc is calibrated.",
